## Part 2: The Telegram Daily Digest — This is a Great Idea

### What You're Building

> A Telegram channel that posts daily: top movers, major news summaries, key points per stock — all AI-generated from your Sentimatix data.

This is perfectly suited for AMD GPU because it uses an **LLM to generate rich narrative text** from structured data you already have.

### Architecture

```
Daily Cron (6PM IST, after market close)
  │
  ├─ 1. Query Supabase → top 10 stocks by sentiment_score delta today
  ├─ 2. Fetch today's news articles for those stocks
  ├─ 3. Spin up AMD GPU Droplet (or use always-on if heavy usage)
  ├─ 4. vLLM serving Llama 3 70B
  ├─ 5. Generate digest (structured prompt → markdown output)
  ├─ 6. Post to Telegram channel via bot API
  └─ 7. Destroy GPU droplet
```

### The Prompt Structure

```python
DAILY_DIGEST_PROMPT = """
You are Sentimatix, an AI financial analyst covering Indian stock markets (NSE/BSE).

Today's date: {date}
Market close: Nifty 50 at {nifty_level} ({nifty_change}%)

Top movers data:
{stock_data}  # JSON: [{stock, sentiment_score, score_delta, top_headlines}]

Write a concise Telegram-formatted daily digest covering:
1. 📈 TOP GAINERS (sentiment) — 2-3 sentences each
2. 📉 TOP LOSERS (sentiment) — 2-3 sentences each  
3. 🔥 KEY THEME OF THE DAY — what story dominated Indian markets today
4. ⚡ WATCH TOMORROW — 1-2 stocks to watch based on momentum

Format for Telegram (use **bold**, bullet points). Keep total under 1500 chars.
DO NOT make price predictions. Report sentiment and news only.
"""
```

### Model Choice for Telegram Digest

| Model | VRAM Needed | Quality | Speed (70 articles) | Cost/Run |
|-------|------------|---------|---------------------|----------|
| Llama 3.1 8B | 16 GB | Good | ~5 sec | ~$0.003 |
| Llama 3.1 70B | 140 GB (fits in MI300X 192GB!) | Excellent | ~30 sec | ~$0.02 |
| Qwen2.5 72B | 144 GB | Excellent, better at structured output | ~35 sec | ~$0.02 |
| Mistral 7B | 14 GB | Good | ~4 sec | ~$0.002 |

**Recommendation**: Start with **Llama 3.1 8B** for daily digests. The MI300X fits it entirely in VRAM. Cost per daily digest: **under 1 cent**. Upgrade to 70B only if output quality isn't good enough.

### vLLM Setup on AMD (OpenAI-compatible API)

```bash
# On GPU droplet — AMD's official vLLM Docker
docker pull rocm/vllm

docker run -it \
  --device=/dev/kfd --device=/dev/dri --group-add video \
  -p 8000:8000 \
  rocm/vllm \
  python -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \
    --model meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \
    --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90
```

```python
# Your Python script calls it like OpenAI — zero new SDK needed
from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(base_url="http://YOUR_DROPLET_IP:8000/v1", api_key="none")

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct",
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": DAILY_DIGEST_PROMPT.format(...)}],
    max_tokens=600
)

digest_text = response.choices[0].message.content
```

```python
# Post to Telegram
import httpx

BOT_TOKEN = "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN"
CHANNEL_ID = "@sentimatix_daily"

httpx.post(
    f"https://api.telegram.org/bot{BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage",
    json={"chat_id": CHANNEL_ID, "text": digest_text, "parse_mode": "Markdown"}
)
```

